      "message": "Hi Jim, I\u0027ve tried to fix these issues. The AA path test failures were because the extractBoundaries process might alter the winding order, so we need to synchronize the direction modification for fOriginalSegment.\n\nThe perspective_clip failure occurred because I accidentally deleted a line of code (fMergeCollinearStackCount \u003d 0 in the splitEdge function) while resolving conflicts.\n\nSome non-AA path failures were due to edge cases in segment splitting. For example, if AB is split into AC and CB, precision loss may cause the x-coordinates of A and C to be the same. In a horizontal comparison (A \u003c B), the vertex order of C would then precede A (C \u003c A \u003c B).Thus, when determining the position of A relative to CB, we cannot use the original edge AB (to which CB belongs), because the three points are collinear (incorrect side judgment mistakenly triggers the mergeCollinearEdges process). We just need to exclude this case.",
